From: Primoz Ajdisek <bigpod@bigpod.si>
Subject: [PATCH] build: skip pathological ChatView React Compiler transform

The native React Compiler transform of ChatView.tsx consumes tens of GiB
and can starve hosted runners. Keep the compiler enabled for other modules;
Vite still handles ordinary JSX transformation for the excluded component.

--- a/apps/web/vite.config.ts
+++ b/apps/web/vite.config.ts
@@ -331,7 +331,14 @@
             ],
           }),
       tanstackRouter({ autoCodeSplitting: true }),
-      react({ compiler: true }),
+      react({
+        compiler: true,
+        exclude: [
+          /\/node_modules\//,
+          // Avoid excessive native compiler memory use in this component.
+          /\/src\/components\/ChatView\.tsx$/,
+        ],
+      }),
       tailwindPlugins(bundledDev),
       warmBundledDevPlugin(),
       bundledDev ? bundledDevStableNamesPlugin() : undefined,
